Stage 4
=======

**Contributors:** David Terrett, David Murphy

Input, auxiliar files and output
--------------------------------

* **Input:**

  + A set of IFU XML files with the targets to be used as central fibres
    included, plus their corresponding guide and calib stars.

* **Auxiliar files:**

  Several auxiliar files are used in this stage. They are described in the
  documentation of the configure tools.

* **Output:**

  + A set of configured (and dithered) IFU XML files.


Software
--------

* *configure_and_dither.py*:
  A set of Python functions that handle the I/O for running configure and dither
  on the provided XML files. This requires that a version of configure is installed,
  and that the user has either installed it in the default location (MacOS) or has
  provided via switch the directory where it is installed.

* *postproc.py*:
  Some functions used for post-processing Configure output whilst development is
  still in progress. We aim to deactiveate these when in production.
  
The following software is not distributed in the IFU repository:

* *xmllint*:
  A tool for formatting the output of the XMLs - particularly useful for standardising
  the attribute order in the XMLs to make reading / comparing them easier. If you do
  not have this installed, you can run configure_and_dither.py with the --nolint switch.

* *configure*:

  The main configure tool, which is used for configuring MOS and mIFU fields for
  WEAVE observations.

* *lifu_configure*:

  A configure tool used for "configuring" LIFU fields for WEAVE observations.

* *dither*:

  A configure tool used for dithering IFU configured fields.

The sources of this software are avalaible in *pos* repo at ING Bitbucket
( https://ingbitbucket.ing.iac.es/projects/WVPOS/repos/pos/browse ), while
compiled files are distributed using a page at ING Confluence
( https://ingconfluence.ing.iac.es:8444/confluence/x/woZM ).

